From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:54:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Export surfaces in the layout of the context that will
 decode into them

GStreamer's va dma-buf allocator opens its decode context first, then
creates and exports every surface of its pool before the first decode,
and keeps those fds for the life of each buffer. A surface exported that
early had no CAPTURE buffer yet, so it got standalone backing from
whichever decoder enumerates first, in NV12 at the surface size with the
64-byte pitch. On the AV1 core that never fits: the core appends its
motion vector buffer to every CAPTURE buffer (hantro_av1_mv_size(), 392 192
bytes at 1920x1088: 3 525 632 bytes against 3 133 440 for the bare NV12
planes). capture_buffer_bind() then found the pre-decode export too small,
left the queue on MMAP ("the pre-decode export does not fit the decode
format") and decoded every frame into buffers the client never saw.
vaav1dec into glimagesink showed a solid green picture at full frame
rate; the exported buffers were 100 % zero.

Allocate pre-decode backing in the context's own layout instead. When an
unbound NV12 surface needs backing and a codec context of the surface's
size exists whose CAPTURE memory is still undecided (or already imports
client dma-bufs), a throwaway open of that context's device is set to the
context's OUTPUT format and to the CAPTURE format the first decode will
select - the same selection, now shared through
v4l2r_context_probe_capture_format() - and the buffer is allocated and
exported there. The first decode then finds a fitting export, imports the
client's dma-bufs, and the decoder writes the picture (and its motion
vectors) into exactly the memory the client holds.

Contexts get a creation serial and an output_ready flag (set once the
decoder is open, cleared first thing in DestroyContext) so the newest
matching context is chosen and a half-built or dying one never is. A
render target's own context is the only candidate for it. Contexts that
decode into their own buffers (FFmpeg: it exports after decoding, MMAP)
and contexts behind a format converter are left alone, as is anything
that would not decode to NV12 (10-bit streams keep the generic P010/PL10
backing). With no matching context the generic allocation runs as
before.

License: GPL-3.0-or-later, like the code it changes (libva-v4l2_request).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
